<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  nl.gewoonsander.podcast-transcribe — transcribe an episode ONLY after Sander
  has actually listened to it. Companion to nl.gewoonsander.podcast-sync.

  NOT INSTALLED AUTOMATICALLY. Daedalus announces runtimes; Sander installs
  them. Install only when he says so:

    sed -e "s|__VAULT__|$PWD|g" -e "s|__PY__|/opt/homebrew/bin/python3|g" \
        -e "s|__HOME__|$HOME|g" \
        Expansions/mypka-cockpit/launchd/nl.gewoonsander.podcast-transcribe.plist.template \
      > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/nl.gewoonsander.podcast-transcribe.plist
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/nl.gewoonsander.podcast-transcribe.plist 2>/dev/null
    launchctl load   ~/Library/LaunchAgents/nl.gewoonsander.podcast-transcribe.plist

  ── ARM IT FIRST, or nothing is safe ────────────────────────────────────────
  Before loading this job, the watermark MUST exist:

    python3 Expansions/mypka-cockpit/scripts/podcast-transcribe-on-watch.py --seed

  Armed 2026-08-19 with 14 already-seen episodes frozen as history. The seed run
  transcribes zero by design — see the script's docstring, guard 1. If the
  watermark is ever missing the script re-seeds and transcribes nothing, so a
  lost state file fails safe, never open.

  ── Why 3600 and an offset from the sync ────────────────────────────────────
  The sync (StartInterval 2700) is what turns an episode "played" in the mirror;
  this job only reads that result. Running it slightly slower than the sync
  means every tick sees a settled mirror instead of racing it. A tick with an
  empty queue costs one read-only sqlite query and exits — no network at all.

  ── Why the perl alarm wrapper ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  Same reason as podcast-sync: the vault sits under an iCloud-backed ~/Documents
  and an open() there can wedge in the kernel indefinitely, and launchd will not
  start a second instance of a job that never exited. 3600 s is generous on
  purpose — a Whisper fallback on a 55-minute episode is legitimately slow.

  ── Why --max 3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Blast-radius bound (guard 4). Well above Sander's real listening rate, far
  below "an archive". Anything above the cap simply waits for the next tick.
-->
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>nl.gewoonsander.podcast-transcribe</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key><array>
    <string>/usr/bin/perl</string>
    <string>-e</string>
    <string>alarm shift; exec @ARGV</string>
    <string>3600</string>
    <string>__PY__</string>
    <string>__VAULT__/Expansions/mypka-cockpit/scripts/podcast-transcribe-on-watch.py</string>
    <string>--run</string>
    <string>--max</string>
    <string>3</string>
    <string>--json</string>
  </array>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>__VAULT__</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key><dict>
    <key>PATH</key><string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>3600</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
  <key>LowPriorityIO</key><true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/mypka-podcast-transcribe.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/mypka-podcast-transcribe.err.log</string>
</dict></plist>
